# tab_breakeven_scoring

**Claim carried:** C3: scoring of the break-even prediction, one row per population (curve), calibrated (spline) arm.

**Shows:** one row per population of breakeven.csv (calibrator `calib_spline`; the synthetic populations are run at several N with one prediction and one measured curve, so they are one row here; N is in breakeven.csv); predicted n* = K/(K-1) d_eff sigma2_res / Delta with the pool-bootstrap interval on real pools (`exact` = synthetic population, no interval); grid = smallest and largest n run; measured crossing = the pair of grid sizes between which the calibrated arm first wins against PPI++ under the pre-fixed rule (`win between a and b`), or `win at the smallest n` (left-censored) or `no win up to n_max` (right-censored); `Scored` = within the pre-fixed factor of 3 in n, only for bracketed rows; `Flag in file` = `pred_within_factor3` as written by analysis, which is 1 for 12 of the 12 censored populations (it counts a censored measurement as within the factor whenever the prediction lies beyond the grid on that side) and is not a confirmation. Grouped as the text: quadratic / shapes / real / stress; longtable. Against the narrower of the two PPI++ variants (`*_best` columns, written for the real datasets only) the bracket, the censoring and the flag of every real dataset are the same as shown.

**How to read:** count the `Scored` column: 11 populations are bracketed, 9 of them within the factor; 10 bracketed synthetic and stress populations, 9 within the factor; real datasets 1 bracketed (0 within the factor), the other 8 censored.

